## Summary
Professor Lee Yong-woo's team at Sahmyook University has scientifically proven the effectiveness of using Virtual Reality (VR) for physical therapy education. Their research demonstrates that VR technology significantly enhances learning outcomes and practical skills in physical therapy training.

## Key Points
- The study provides scientific validation for VR's effectiveness in physical therapy education.
- VR-based training improves educational outcomes and practical application in healthcare.
- This research supports the integration of advanced technologies into medical education curricula.


